# Line-ending policy: every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on
# every platform and regardless of core.autocrlf. Byte-level hashes (the skill
# contract audit corpus hash, BER frozen artifacts and manifests) are computed
# over on-disk bytes, so a CRLF checkout would otherwise produce different
# hashes and a "dirty" working tree on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts stay LF: Windows PowerShell 5.1 and pwsh both accept LF.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF (none are tracked today).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary formats: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary

